isruption":[0,0,0,0.0]},"move":{"r1":0.0267,"r5":0.0152,"r1_spy":0.0315,"r5_spy":0.0422}}],"quotes":[{"c":"KRG 2019 Q2","e":"krg","d":"2019-08-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Thomas K. McGowan","x":"So I do think long-term, all of them feel this will be healthy for the industry to provide a much greater hedge in the event of tariff situations like this, but to date, we have not talked about it specifically on lease rates, TI, etc.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/06/kite-realty-group-trust-krg-q2-2019-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"KRG 2019 Q3","e":"krg","d":"2019-11-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John A. Kite","x":"There's a cost savings there in a lot of different ways.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/06/kite-realty-group-trust-krg-q3-2019-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"KRG 2019 Q3","e":"krg","d":"2019-11-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Daniel Santos","x":"Just keeping with that sort of tenant theme there was an article this morning about Kroger reporting strong results just after following their sort of two-year restructuring plan.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/06/kite-realty-group-trust-krg-q3-2019-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"KRG 2019 Q4","e":"krg","d":"2020-02-19","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Thomas K. Mcgowan","x":"It's important to note that the midpoint of our guidance assumes we received no additional rent from any tenant that was vacated or filed for bankruptcy, including Dress Barn, Pier 1, Bar Louie, A.C. Moore, Earth Fare, and Frank's Theater.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/19/kite-realty-group-trust-krg-q4-2019-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"KRG 2020 Q1","e":"krg","d":"2020-05-07","l":"theater","r":"analyst","s":"Alexander Goldfarb","x":"First is, John apart from your gentle persuasive voice, you guys did manage to get rent collections from a number of tenants like movie theaters that were closed and other ones like soft goods and personal service etc, where the bulk were closed, and yet your rent collections vastly exceeded.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/07/kite-realty-group-trust-krg-q1-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"KRG 2020 Q2","e":"krg","d":"2020-08-06","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"John A. Kite","x":"With respect to the remaining 6% that are closed, 3% have not been able to reopen due to local restrictions, including some of our gym and theater tenants.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/06/kite-realty-group-trust-krg-q2-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"KRG 2020 Q2","e":"krg","d":"2020-08-06","l":"theater","r":"analyst","s":"Alexander Goldfarb","x":"And then the other thing that just continues to be impressive is the fact that your movie theaters last quarter and this quarter, even though they're all closed, they're still like a good amount are paying rent, which is just really impressive.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/06/kite-realty-group-trust-krg-q2-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"KRG 2020 Q4","e":"krg","d":"2021-02-12","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"John A. Kite","x":"Sometimes you would say well why -- you collected more theater rent than almost anybody or it seems like you're fitness guys are paying a little more.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/12/kite-realty-group-trust-krg-q4-2020-earnings-call/"},{"c":"KRG 2020 Q4","e":"krg","d":"2021-02-12","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Heath R. Fear","x":"Excluding the one-time impact of severance charges related to some management changes, FFO as adjusted is $0.33 per share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/12/kite-realty-group-trust-krg-q4-2020-earnings-call/"},{"c":"KRG 2021 Q1","e":"krg","d":"2021-04-30","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Heath R. Fear","x":"We are raising our 2021 guidance of FFO as adjusted to be between $1.26 and $1.34 per share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/kite-realty-group-trust-krg-q1-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"KRG 2021 Q2","e":"krg","d":"2021-08-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"John A. Kite","x":"And I think over time, that diluted the pricing power.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/03/kite-realty-group-trust-reit-krg-q2-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"KRG 2021 Q2","e":"krg","d":"2021-08-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"John A. Kite","x":"I think this has a longer, maybe a more gradual gestation period in that, Wesley, and that this pricing power is a little different.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/03/kite-realty-group-trust-reit-krg-q2-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"KRG 2021 Q2","e":"krg","d":"2021-08-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John A. Kite","x":"And it was in the light of a lot of moving parts as it related to increasing cost out on the supply chain, which has moderated significantly.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/03/kite-realty-group-trust-reit-krg-q2-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"KRG 2021 Q2","e":"krg","d":"2021-08-03","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Heath Fear","x":"We are raising our 2021 guidance of FFO as adjusted to be between $1.29 and $1.35 per share, an increase of $0.02 at the midpoint.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/03/kite-realty-group-trust-reit-krg-q2-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"KRG 2022 Q2","e":"krg","d":"2022-08-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"John Kite","x":"But in terms of what we're seeing and what we're hearing every day, I mean, there's absolute demand for the space, which is the friction that's creating the pricing power.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/08/03/kite-realty-group-trust-krg-q2-2022-earnings-call/"},{"c":"KRG 2022 Q2","e":"krg","d":"2022-08-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John Kite","x":"We monitor everybody -- 